{
    "background_story": "Bruce was a renowned civil engineer with a passion for building bridges. Growing up near the iconic Golden Gate Bridge, he was fascinated by the way it connected two landmasses, fostering growth and unity. After completing his studies, Bruce traveled the world, designing and constructing bridges in diverse landscapes. From the suspension bridges of Japan to the arch bridges of Europe, he left his mark on the global infrastructure. However, his most notable project was the rehabilitation of a historic bridge in his hometown, which had been damaged in a natural disaster. Bruce's innovative design not only restored the bridge but also transformed it into a vibrant public space, earning him widespread acclaim. Through his work, Bruce built more than just bridges \u2013 he built connections between communities and cultures.",
